  "result": "`RegExp.prototype.source` is implemented in `crates/kahvi-builtins/src/reg_exp/prototype_get_source.rs`. All 24 runs under `built-ins/RegExp/prototype/source/` pass (up from 6), and clippy and `cargo fmt --check` are clean.\n\nSince no `EscapeRegExpPattern` helper exists in the engine, I wrote it as a private function in the same file, as the ticket allows. It escapes unescaped `/` and the four line terminators, and it returns `\"(?:)\"` for an empty pattern. Its output does not depend on the flags, because the escapes it produces are valid in every pattern mode, so the flags are not passed to it. Other built-ins that need this operation (for example `RegExp.prototype.toString`, if it is implemented separately) would need it moved into `support/regexp.rs`.\n\nBLOCKED: none",
